Step 0 supports a build, but as Track B—not Track A. The paper’s hard theorem applies when the number of shuffled strings is unrestricted, while this constructed distribution has a linear-time complement-hashing algorithm. At the shipping preset that mechanical route scans tens of thousands of symbols; the planted power-of-two projection reduces the no-tool route to 273 symbol operations. I’m implementing that distinction explicitly rather than claiming the inverse-planted distribution inherits NP-hardness.
